# Production build config, committed on purpose.
#
# Vite substitutes this at BUILD time, so it has to exist before the build runs -- setting it in a
# host's dashboard afterwards does nothing until the next deploy, and the symptom is a live site
# that reports the model offline while pointing at localhost.
#
# Committing it rather than configuring it in Vercel keeps the deploy reproducible from the repo
# alone: clone, push, and the build points at the right backend. This is not a secret -- it is a
# public endpoint, already readable in the shipped JavaScript.
VITE_API_URL=https://ivansost--ai-visualizer-web.modal.run
